{
  "paraphrase": "For all functions a and b from the natural numbers to the natural numbers, if for every natural number n, a(n) is positive, and the sum of 1 over a(n) is summable, then the limit of b(n) divided by n as n approaches infinity is zero, where b(n) is defined as the cardinality of the set of natural numbers k such that a(k) is less than or equal to n."
}
